  "full_text": "You know, sometimes I quote this song because it's a useful concept. When I was just a little boy, I asked my mother, what will I be? Will I be handsome? Will I be rich? Here's what she said to me. Hey, sirrah, sirrah, whatever will be, will be. The future's not ours to see. Que sera, sera. What will be, will be. Let's see if I can do a little better job. So like, yeah, you don't want to intimidate amateurs. When I was just a little, when I was just a little boy, I asked my mother, what will I be? Will I be handsome? Will I be rich? Here's what she said to me. Que sera, sera. Whatever will be, will be. The future's not ours to see. Que sera, sera. What will be, will be. That's it. As for the beauty of his ornament, he set it in majesty, but they made the images of their abominations and their detestable things therein. Therefore I have set it far from them. I will give it into the hands of the strangers for a prey, and into the wicked of the earth for a spoil, and they shall pollute it. My face I will turn also from them, and they shall pollute my secret place, and the robbers shall enter into it and defile it.",
